# Where the parser ignored an allocation's failure and went on, in three
# functions: a child definition whose constant-pool add failed
# (js_create_function asserted on its missing slot, ending the program); a
# closure-variable add in resolve_scope_var (its -1 used as an index,
# emitted as nothing, or taken by resolve_variables as the next position
# and read at bc_buf[-1]); an `arguments` or function-name add there (its
# -1 captured as a wild argument slot of an enclosing function, or, in the
# function's own scope, looked up as a global: a wrong answer); and
# get_lvalue reading a failed bytecode buffer as a bad assignment target
# (a SyntaxError). Each now throws out of memory through the existing fail
# path. resolve_labels' output buffer, the tokenizer lookahead, the
# pseudo-variable adds and add_eval_variables are not covered (DEBTS.md).
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
